usage: c2-controls.py [-h] [--root ROOT] --counter COUNTER [--rubric RUBRIC]
                      [--rev REV] [--freeze FREEZE] [--work WORK] [--out OUT]
                      [--json-out JSON_OUT] [--mode {auto,dev,real}]
                      [--ctl CTL] [--fitness] [--fitness-limit FITNESS_LIMIT]
                      [--dev-variant {stale,consistent}]

R44-C2 controls: CTL-C2-0/1/2/3 against the frozen counter.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --root ROOT           lane root (real mode)
  --counter COUNTER     path to c2-counter.py
  --rubric RUBRIC       path to the frozen c2-rubric.json
  --rev REV             measured revision
  --freeze FREEZE       freeze revision
  --work WORK           scratch directory
  --out OUT             directory for the per-control receipts
  --json-out JSON_OUT   summary receipt
  --mode {auto,dev,real}
  --ctl CTL
  --fitness             run the per-entry fitness gate: every rubric entry is
                        shown able to fail on its own statement (one asserted-
                        value mutation per entry)
  --fitness-limit FITNESS_LIMIT
                        score only the first N entries (a bounded sample; the
                        receipt says how many were scored)
  --dev-variant {stale,consistent}
                        dev fixture shape: `stale` = the fixture statement is
                        wrong (the census reports a mismatch, the do-nothing
                        control fails); `consistent` = the statement is right
                        (the census reports zero mismatches — the honest-stop
                        signal for R44-C2)
